From: MaSi-OS <masies@local>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom-q6v5: silence ADSP handover IRQ spam

On SM8550 ADSP the firmware keeps asserting the handover interrupt after
the AP has already handled it. Linux 7.2 logs dev_err on every spurious
edge (~5/s), flooding dmesg/journal.

Disable the handover IRQ after the first successful handover and drop the
duplicate error print (the IRQ should not fire again once masked).

Signed-off-by: MaSi-OS <masies@local>

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
@@ -164,8 +164,7 @@ static irqreturn_t q6v5_handover_interrupt(int irq, void *data)
 	struct qcom_q6v5 *q6v5 = data;
 
 	if (q6v5->handover_issued) {
-		dev_err(q6v5->dev, "Handover signaled, but it already happened\n");
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
 
 	if (q6v5->handover)
@@ -175,6 +174,7 @@ static irqreturn_t q6v5_handover_interrupt(int irq, void *data)
 	icc_set_bw(q6v5->path, 0, 0);
 
 	q6v5->handover_issued = true;
+	disable_irq(q6v5->handover_irq);
 
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
 }
